// Test simfile with hand-worked durations and foot simulations, for calibrating ddr-trainer's
// chart analyzer (src/chart_analyzer.rs), whose tests check the values below. Generated by
// test_resources/make_test_simfiles.py, so edit that instead of this.
//
// One BPM (120, so quarter notes are 0.5 s apart and 8ths 0.25 s), no stops.
//   - the duration runs from the chart's first object (a note, mine or hold end) to its last,
//     and the active ratio is the fraction of it between notes at most 1 s apart, or holding
//   - the foot simulation splits the notes into segments at gaps longer than 0.5 s, so quarter
//     notes stay in one. Each segment starts with the feet at home (left foot on Left, right
//     on Right), then alternates feet, except that the same foot steps a jack and the other
//     foot steps while one holds. It's run starting with each foot, keeping the less awkward
//     (fewer crossovers, laterals and spins in all, the left foot on a tie)
//   - a crossover is a step into one foot on the far side's arrow and the other on Up or Down,
//     a lateral a step into the feet swapped (left on Right, right on Left), a half spin a turn
//     of 180 to 359 degrees through facing away from the screen, and a full spin 360 degrees
//   - the wrong-foot penalty is how many more of those in all starting each segment with the
//     worse foot gives than starting with the better one, per note. It splits segments at gaps
//     longer than 0.25 s instead, so quarter notes here are each a segment of their own
//
//   chart      duration  active  crossovers  laterals  half spins  full spins  wrong foot
//   Beginner   0         0       0           0         0           0           0           nothing in it
//   Easy       7         1/2     0           0         0           0           0           duration
//   Medium     3.5       4/7     2           0         0           0           0           breaks reset
//   Hard       2.75      6/11    0           0         0           0           2/8         easier foot
//   Challenge  6         7/12    1           0         0           1           4/16        realistic mix
//
// Easy: 2 s to 9 s (a mine), active from 2 s to 5.5 s (quarter notes, then a hold).
// Medium: two crossovers in quarter notes (Left, Down, Right), with a 1.5 s break between them.
//   Without the feet going home in the break, the second would start with the right foot on
//   Left, a lateral. Each note is a segment of its own at 0.25 s, so there's no wrong foot.
// Hard: Up, Left, Up, Left crosses over if the left foot starts, so the right foot does, and
//   after a break Up, Right, Up, Right crosses over if the right foot starts, so the left does.
//   That's 1 more with the worse foot in each: a wrong-foot penalty of 2 over 8 notes.
// Challenge: Left, Down, Right, Up, Left, Down in 8ths is a crossover and a full spin starting
//   with the left foot (with the right, 2 crossovers and a full spin). Then Up, Left, Up, Left
//   as in Hard, then a hold on Left with Down, Up, Down stepped by the right foot under it.
//   At 0.25 s, that last segment splits in two before the final Up. Starting with the right foot
//   crosses over in both: the left foot takes Down under the hold, then steps Right while the
//   right foot is on Up. With 1 each from the first two, the penalty is 4 over 16 notes.
#TITLE:Footing Stats;
#ARTIST:ddr-trainer;
#MUSIC:footing_stats.ogg;
#OFFSET:0.000000;
#BPMS:0.000=120.000;
#STOPS:;

//---------------dance-single - nothing in it----------------
#NOTES:
     dance-single:
     nothing in it:
     Beginner:
     1:
     0.412,0.356,0.250,0.100,0.000:
// measure 0: empty
0000
0000
0000
0000
,  // measure 1: empty
0000
0000
0000
0000
;

//---------------dance-single - duration----------------
#NOTES:
     dance-single:
     duration:
     Easy:
     2:
     0.412,0.356,0.250,0.100,0.000:
// measure 0: empty
0000
0000
0000
0000
,  // measure 1: quarter notes from 2 s
1000
0100
0010
0001
,  // measure 2: a hold from 4 s to 5.5 s
2000
0000
0000
3000
,  // measure 3: empty, a break
0000
0000
0000
0000
,  // measure 4: a tap at 8 s, and a mine at 9 s that ends the chart
1000
0000
000M
0000
,  // measure 5: empty
0000
0000
0000
0000
;

